+# Shorter session names
+
+Pablo requested a simpler title after reviewing the attitude pilot on 28 October 2026.
+The title now shows **role · attitude — project**. Subject focus stays in the conversation receipt and Status.
+
+![All four session fields remain in the receipt; the shorter title shows role, attitude and project.](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-focus/images/session-fields-simple.svg)
+
+## Naming rules
+
+| Situation | Display |
+| --- | --- |
+| Governance, no selected attitude | `00 Governance · NoAttitude — SpeakerCoach` |
+| Architecture, Black attitude | `05 High-Level Architecture · Black — SpeakerCoach` |
+| No selected subject | `Focus: NoFocus` in the reply and receipt; omitted from the title. |
+
+`Off` remains an accepted input alias, but the resulting label is NoAttitude. A known unset subject formerly recorded as None becomes NoFocus.
+Unknown history stays Unknown. Subject-only changes no longer rename the chat; different subjects can legitimately share a title.
+Skills, discovery templates, usage guidance and acceptance scenarios use the new convention. Stable thread IDs still identify distinct chats.
+
+## Verification and preservation
+
+Project structure verification passes. The package checker reports only the same eight pre-existing external presentation links.
+The updated SVG was rendered and visually inspected at 720 px. This instruction-only correction adds no implementation test.
+Native renaming acknowledged the new Governance title and both existing Architecture test titles; this chat's exact title was also read back.
+The two test chats retain their separate Security and Performance receipts. No new chats, peer messages or role/attitude selections were made.
+Previous pilot evidence remains historical; this review supersedes its naming convention without rewriting its results.
+Existing uncommitted work was preserved. Application code, sprint state, hooks and approval decisions were not changed; no commit or push occurred.
+
+[Naming contract](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-focus/rename-chat.md) · [Incremental diff from the pre-edit working tree](02.9-review-short-session-names.diff) · [Previous pilot](02.8-review-attitude-and-session-naming.md)
